.TITLE "mv"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Moves or renames files and directories. It is the standard way to reorganize __files__ and change their __names__ within the filesystem.

.DIV "TLDR"
**mv source destination**
Moves a file or directory to a new location or renames it.
> __source__ the original file | __destination__ the target path

**mv -i source destination**
Prompts for confirmation before overwriting an existing file.
> __-i__ interactive flag | __source__ the original file | __destination__ target path

**mv -n source destination**
Prevents overwriting an existing file at the destination.
> __-n__ no clobber flag | __source__ original file | __destination__ target path

**mv -u source destination**
Only moves the file if the source is newer than the destination.
> __-u__ update flag | __source__ original file | __destination__ target path

**mv -v source destination**
Displays a message for every file that is moved or renamed.
> __-v__ verbose flag | __source__ original file | __destination__ target path

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Renaming a file is simply a __move__ operation within the same directory. To protect against accidental data loss, consider using the __-n__ flag when moving files into a folder that may already contain files with the same name.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:cp** **linux:rm** **linux:rename**

documentation: __https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/mv__
